M3-c153 L09 None 
  F: What is eigenvalue clipping of a real symmetric matrix A at a floor epsilon >= 0? 
  B: Assuming F1 to F4 of Lesson 4, with A = Q Lambda Q^T a spectral decomposition, the matrix Q diag(max(lambda_1, epsilon), …, max(lambda_n, epsilon)) Q^T. Clipping at zero replaces each negative eigenvalue by zero (Definition 3.1). 
  LESSON: 
