M3-c180 L05 T 
  F: For real symmetric positive semidefinite matrices A and C and c >= 0, are A + C and cA positive semidefinite? 
  B: Yes. x^T(A + C)x = x^T A x + x^T C x >= 0 and x^T(cA)x = c x^T A x >= 0 for every x, and both matrices are symmetric (Proposition 1.6). 
  LESSON: 
M3-c019 L01 C 
  F: In Lab 1, how many of the 200 seeded lists of four vectors in R^3 are independent? 
  B: 0 of 200 (Lab 1 output). Corollary 3.6 predicts this count, because every list of four vectors in R^3 is dependent. It describes the listed draws only. 
